1. A cable bolt for supporting a rock mass, comprising:  
a multi-strand steel cable extending along a longitudinal axis and having a first end portion, a second end portion, and an intermediate load-transfer portion configured to be grouted in a borehole formed in the rock mass, the multi-strand steel cable comprising a plurality of helically wound steel strands; and  
an end fixture secured to the first end portion of the multi-strand steel cable and configured to couple the multi-strand steel cable to a bearing plate, nut, barrel-and-wedge assembly, or other rock-support anchoring component;  
wherein at least one of the steel strands is formed from a steel alloy consisting essentially of, in weight percent: carbon from 0.15 to 0.45%, manganese from 0.30 to 2.00%, silicon from 0.10 to 1.20%, chromium from 10.0 to 18.0%, nickel from 1.0 to 8.0%, molybdenum from 0.10 to 3.00%, nitrogen from 0.01 to 0.25%, copper from 0 to 2.00%, vanadium from 0 to 0.30%, niobium from 0 to 0.20%, titanium from 0 to 0.20%, phosphorus not greater than 0.040%, sulfur not greater than 0.030%, and a balance of iron and unavoidable impurities;  
wherein the steel alloy has a corrosion-resistant multiphase microstructure comprising, by volume, martensite from 35% to 85%, retained austenite from 5% to 45%, and ferrite from 0% to 30%, with any carbides, nitrides, or carbonitrides collectively being not greater than 10%; and  
wherein the multi-strand steel cable has a tensile strength sufficient to place the cable bolt in load-bearing engagement with the rock mass when the end fixture is tensioned relative to the borehole.

1. A mining cable bolt comprising a plurality of twisted steel wires, wherein at least one of the twisted steel wires comprises, in weight percent:

- carbon: 0.20 to 0.95;
- silicon: 0.5 to 2.0;
- manganese: 0.40 to 1.0;
- chromium: 0 to 1.0;
- sulfur: not more than 0.025;
- phosphorus: not more than 0.025;
- balance iron and unavoidable impurities;

wherein the at least one twisted steel wire has a retained austenite content of 4 to 25 percent.

1. A rock reinforcement cable bolt for installation in a borehole formed in a rock mass, the cable bolt comprising:  

a multi-strand cable having a first end configured to be anchored within the borehole and a second end configured to be positioned adjacent an opening of the borehole;  

a fixture mounted at or adjacent the second end of the multi-strand cable and configured to bear against a surface of the rock mass directly or through a bearing plate, thereby applying a retaining load to the rock mass;  

wherein the multi-strand cable comprises a plurality of helically wound steel wires; and  

wherein each of the steel wires is formed from a high-strength steel alloy comprising, by weight, 0.70 to 1.10% carbon, 0.30 to 1.20% manganese, 0.10 to 0.60% silicon, up to 0.50% chromium, up to 0.20% vanadium, up to 0.10% molybdenum, balance iron and unavoidable impurities, and has a drawn pearlitic microstructure comprising elongated pearlite colonies with cementite lamellae aligned generally along a longitudinal direction of the wire.

